## Why This Is Asked

Assess practical blind source separation pipeline design under real-time, network-induced constraints for collaboration tools deployed at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming BSS with time-varying mixing matrices
- Synchronization strategies for asynchronous inputs and packet loss
- Joint diagonalization versus per-bin ICA trade-offs
- Latency budgeting and robustness to network jitter
- Evaluation methodology using SDR/SIR metrics plus perceptual validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: online BSS for 2 sources, 4 mics
function onlineBSS(micFrames) {
  // Synchronize misaligned frames
  const syncedFrames = synchronizeStreams(micFrames);

  // STFT processing
  const stftFrames = syncedFrames.map(frame => stft(frame));

  // Estimate time-varying mixing matrix
  const mixingMatrix = estimateMixingMatrix(stftFrames);

  // Apply spatially varying whitening
  const whitened = spatialWhitening(stftFrames, mixingMatrix);

  // Joint diagonalization for source separation
  const separatedSources = jointDiagonalization(whitened);

  return separatedSources;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to handle realistic failure modes in deployed audio systems—microphone dropouts and dynamic speaker counts are common in video calls and live events. The interviewer wants to see that you can design for robustness rather than just nominal conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Online ICA with time-varying channel count and dimensionality
- Masked whitening to handle missing channels without retraining
- Cross-bin permutation alignment using angular consistency
- On-device ground-truth evaluation using play-and-record setups

## Follow-up Questions
- **How would you handle highly correlated sources?** Consider geometric constraints from the microphone array geometry, incorporate direction-of-arrival cues as prior information, or relax the independence assumption toward spatial clustering.
- **How would you trade off latency vs. separation quality?** Increase the STFT frame size for better frequency resolution, reduce overlap for lower computational load, or use a lookahead buffer with causal post-filtering to improve quality at the cost of slight additional delay.

